<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />

		<title>
			Interactive Visual Analytics for Type 1 Diabetes | Marco Thoma
		</title>

		<meta
			name="description"
			content="A Master's project exploring similarity search and interactive visual analytics for Type 1 diabetes health data."
		/>

		<link rel="canonical" href="https://marcothoma.com/work/type-1-diabetes" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<meta name="theme-color" content="#101312" />
	</head>

	<body>
		<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">
			Skip to main content
		</a>
		<header class="project-header">
			<a class="logo" href="/">MT</a>

			<a class="back-link" href="/#work">
				<span>←</span>
				Back to work
			</a>
		</header>

		<main id="main-content">

			<!-- HERO -->
			<section class="project-hero">
				<div class="hero-copy">
					<p class="eyebrow">
						MASTER'S PROJECT · INTERACTIVE VISUAL DATA ANALYTICS
					</p>

					<h1>
						Similarity Search in Health Data through
						Interactive Visual Data Analytics
					</h1>

					<p class="hero-intro">
						A web application designed to help people with Type 1 diabetes
						explore their health data, identify comparable situations and
						better understand patterns through similarity search and
						interactive visualizations.
					</p>

                    <div class="hero-concept">
                        <span>CORE IDEA</span>

                        <p>
                            Explore.<br />
                            Search.<br />
                            Compare.
                        </p>
                    </div>

					<div class="project-meta">
						<div>
							<span>Role</span>
							<p>Frontend Development</p>
						</div>

						<div>
							<span>Team</span>
							<p>5 people</p>
						</div>

						<div>
							<span>Focus</span>
							<p>Visual Analytics · HCI · Health Data</p>
						</div>

						<div>
							<span>Frontend</span>
							<p>React · TypeScript · D3</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<figure class="hero-image">
					<img
						src="/images/projects/masters-project.png"
						alt="Overview screen of the Type 1 diabetes visual analytics application"
					/>
				</figure>
			</section>


			<!-- CONTEXT -->
			<section class="content-section">
				<div class="section-number">01 / CONTEXT</div>

				<div class="section-content">
					<h2>
						Making complex diabetes data easier to explore.
					</h2>

					<div class="two-column-text">
						<p>
							People with Type 1 diabetes generate large amounts of
							time-based health data. Glucose levels are influenced by
							multiple contextual factors such as insulin, carbohydrate
							intake, physical activity and sleep, making it difficult to
							understand why similar situations may lead to different
							outcomes.
						</p>

						<p>
							Our project explored how interactive visual analytics and
							similarity search could help users investigate these
							relationships. Rather than only tracking individual values,
							the application allows users to search for comparable
							situations across their data and inspect the factors that
							contributed to those similarities.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>


			<!-- ROLE -->
			<section class="content-section muted-section">
				<div class="section-number">02 / MY ROLE</div>

				<div class="section-content">
					<h2>
						Frontend development in a five-person team.
					</h2>

					<p class="wide-copy">
						The project was developed by a team of five. I worked on the
						frontend together with one other team member, contributing to
						the implementation of the user-facing application and its
						interactive visualizations.
					</p>

					<p class="wide-copy secondary-copy">
						The frontend work was collaborative, so I present it here as a
						shared contribution rather than attributing individual
						components exclusively to one person.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>


			<!-- PROCESS -->
			<section class="content-section">
				<div class="section-number">03 / PROCESS</div>

				<div class="section-content">
					<h2>
						From user needs to an interactive prototype.
					</h2>

					<div class="process-grid">
						<div class="process-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<h3>Research</h3>

							<p>
								We reviewed existing diabetes-management and visual
								analytics tools to understand current approaches and
								identify opportunities for deeper pattern exploration.
							</p>
						</div>

						<div class="process-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<h3>Understand</h3>

							<p>
								Three people with Type 1 diabetes were interviewed to
								understand their needs, how they explore their data and
								what similarity means in the context of diabetes
								management.
							</p>
						</div>

						<div class="process-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<h3>Prototype</h3>

							<p>
								Insights were translated into user tasks and interface
								concepts. We used Figma and design sessions to explore
								ways of combining search controls, visualizations and
								detailed data views.
							</p>
						</div>

						<div class="process-item">
							<span>04</span>
							<h3>Refine</h3>

							<p>
								After feedback on an initial prototype, the interface
								was redesigned from two separate screens into a more
								consistent single-screen workflow that adapts after a
								search.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>


			<!-- SIMILARITY SEARCH -->
			<section class="feature-section">
				<div class="feature-copy">
					<p class="eyebrow">CONFIGURABLE SEARCH</p>

					<h2>
						Users define what “similar” means.
					</h2>

					<p>
						The search can be configured according to the user's
						priorities. Individual health features can be weighted and
						different distance metrics can be selected, allowing the
						search to reflect different interpretations of similarity.
					</p>

					<p>
						The application supports Euclidean distance, correlation,
						Dynamic Time Warping and weighted combinations of multiple
						metrics.
					</p>
				</div>

				<figure class="feature-image small-image">
					<img
						src="/images/projects/type-1-diabetes/similarity-settings.png"
						alt="Similarity search settings allowing users to select health features, distance metrics and feature weights."
					/>

					<figcaption>
						Similarity search settings with adjustable feature
						weights and distance metrics.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</section>


			<!-- SOLUTION -->
			<section class="content-section muted-section">
				<div class="section-number">04 / SOLUTION</div>

				<div class="section-content">
					<h2>
						Exploration, search and comparison in one interface.
					</h2>

					<p class="wide-copy">
						The final application combines multiple linked
						visualizations. Before a search, users can explore the dataset
						and inspect individual days. After selecting a query time
						range, the application searches for comparable situations and
						reconfigures the interface to present ranked results and
						comparison views.
					</p>

					<div class="feature-list">
						<div>
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Explore multidimensional health data</p>
						</div>

						<div>
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Define a query time range</p>
						</div>

						<div>
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Configure similarity criteria</p>
						</div>

						<div>
							<span>04</span>
							<p>Inspect ranked matching situations</p>
						</div>

						<div>
							<span>05</span>
							<p>Compare selected results against the query</p>
						</div>

						<div>
							<span>06</span>
							<p>Understand feature contributions to similarity</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>


			<!-- SEARCH RESULT -->
			<section class="visual-section">
				<div class="visual-heading">
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">AFTER THE SEARCH</p>

						<h2>
							Results adapt the entire analytics workspace.
						</h2>
					</div>

					<p>
						Once the search is executed, the interface makes room for
						ranked matches while the surrounding visualizations update to
						represent the search results.
					</p>
				</div>

				<figure class="large-visual">
					<img
						src="/images/projects/type-1-diabetes/search-results.png"
						alt="Similarity search results showing ranked matching time periods and visualizations of the selected health data."
					/>

					<figcaption>
						Application overview after executing a similarity search.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</section>


			<!-- COMPARISON -->
			<section class="visual-section comparison-section">
				<div class="visual-heading">
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow">COMPARISON</p>

						<h2>
							From ranked matches to detailed comparison.
						</h2>
					</div>

					<p>
						Users can select up to three search results for comparison.
						Their time-series data is overlaid against the original query,
						making differences and similarities across individual features
						easier to inspect.
					</p>
				</div>

				<figure class="large-visual">
					<img
						src="/images/projects/type-1-diabetes/comparison-results.png"
						alt="Comparison view displaying multiple similarity search results side by side for detailed visual analysis."
					/>

					<figcaption>
						Three selected similarity-search results compared with
						the original query.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</section>


			<!-- TECH STACK -->
			<section class="content-section dark-section">
				<div class="section-number">05 / TECHNOLOGY</div>

				<div class="section-content">
					<h2>
						Technology stack.
					</h2>

					<div class="tech-grid">
						<div>
							<span>Frontend</span>
							<h3>React</h3>
							<p>TypeScript · D3 · Electron Forge</p>
						</div>

						<div>
							<span>Backend</span>
							<h3>Python</h3>
							<p>FastAPI</p>
						</div>

						<div>
							<span>Data</span>
							<h3>PostgreSQL</h3>
							<p>TimescaleDB</p>
						</div>

						<div>
							<span>Workflow</span>
							<h3>GitLab</h3>
							<p>Git · Docker · Figma</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>


			<!-- OUTCOME -->
			<section class="content-section outcome-section">
				<div class="section-number">06 / OUTCOME</div>

				<div class="section-content">
					<h2>
						A working prototype and a foundation for further evaluation.
					</h2>

					<div class="two-column-text">
						<p>
							The project resulted in a functional application that
							combines configurable similarity search with interactive
							visual analytics. It demonstrates how complex
							multidimensional health data can be transformed into an
							explorable workflow rather than presented only as isolated
							measurements.
						</p>

						<p>
							A formal user evaluation was planned as the next stage of
							the project. This would involve people with Type 1 diabetes
							and visual analytics expertise using the application,
							thinking aloud while completing tasks and providing
							feedback for subsequent iterations.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="takeaway">
						<p class="eyebrow">PERSONAL TAKEAWAY</p>

						<p>
							The project gave me practical experience working on a
							collaborative frontend, developing visualization-rich
							interfaces and translating a technically complex analytical
							concept into a user-facing digital product.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>


			<!-- NEXT PROJECT -->
			<section class="next-project">
				<p>BACK TO SELECTED WORK</p>

				<a href="/work">
					View projects
					<span>→</span>
				</a>
			</section>

		</main>

		<footer>
			<p class="footer-site">marcothoma.com</p>

			<div class="footer-center">
				<p>Designed & built by Marco Thoma</p>

				<div class="footer-legal">
					<a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
					<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
					<a href="/legal-notice">Legal Notice</a>
				</div>
			</div>

			<p class="footer-copy">© 2026</p>
		</footer>
	</body>
</html>


<style>
	:root {
		--background: #f7f7f5;
		--surface: #ffffff;
		--text: #101312;
		--muted: #626966;
		--light-muted: #858b88;
		--border: #d9ddda;
		--accent: #deac53;
		--accent-text: #8f6210;
		--page-padding: clamp(28px, 4vw, 76px);
	}

	* {
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	html {
		scroll-behavior: smooth;
	}

	body {
		margin: 0;
		background: var(--background);
		color: var(--text);
		font-family:
			Arial,
			Helvetica,
			sans-serif;
	}

	img {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
	}

	a {
		color: inherit;
	}

	.skip-link {
		position: fixed;
		top: 12px;
		left: 50%;
		z-index: 9999;
		padding: 12px 16px;
		background: #101312;
		color: #ffffff;
		font-size: 13px;
		font-weight: 700;
		text-decoration: none;
		white-space: nowrap;
		transform: translate(-50%, -150%);
		transition: transform 0.2s ease;
	}

	.skip-link:focus {
		transform: translate(-50%, 0);
	}

	/* HEADER */

	.project-header {
		height: 84px;
		padding: 0 var(--page-padding);
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.logo {
		font-size: 22px;
		font-weight: 750;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.back-link {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 10px;
		font-size: 12px;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: color 0.2s ease;
	}

	.back-link span {
		color: var(--accent);
		transition: transform 0.2s ease;
	}

	.back-link:hover {
		color: var(--accent);
	}

	.back-link:hover span {
		transform: translateX(-4px);
	}


	/* HERO */

	.project-hero {
		padding: 90px var(--page-padding) 0;
	}

	.hero-copy {
		max-width: 1150px;
		margin-bottom: 65px;
	}

	.eyebrow {
		margin: 0 0 22px;
		color: var(--light-muted);
		font-size: 10px;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
	}

	.project-hero h1 {
		max-width: 1100px;
		margin: 0;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(46px, 6vw, 88px);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.02;
		letter-spacing: -0.045em;
	}

	.hero-intro {
		max-width: 760px;
		margin: 34px 0 0;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 17px;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

    .hero-copy {
        position: relative;
        max-width: 1150px;
        margin-bottom: 65px;
    }

    .hero-concept {
        position: absolute;
        top: 35px;
        left: calc(100% + 120px);
        width: 220px;
        padding-top: 18px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--accent);
    }

    .hero-concept span {
        color: var(--light-muted);
        font-size: 9px;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    }

    .hero-concept p {
        margin: 16px 0 0;
        font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
        font-size: 28px;
        line-height: 1.3;
    }

	.project-meta {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
		gap: 30px;
		margin-top: 55px;
		padding-top: 26px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.project-meta span {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
        color: var(--light-muted);
        font-size: 10px;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.15em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.project-meta p {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 15px;
        line-height: 1.5;
	}

	.hero-image {
        max-width: 1650px;
        margin: 0 auto;
		margin-bottom: 32px;
        overflow: hidden;
        border-radius: 4px 4px 0 0;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-bottom: 0;
        background: white;
	}

	.hero-image img {
        width: 100%;
        height: auto;
        object-fit: contain;
	}


	/* STANDARD CONTENT SECTION */

	.content-section {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(130px, 0.23fr) 1fr;
		gap: 60px;
		padding: 110px var(--page-padding);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.section-number {
		padding-top: 9px;
		color: var(--light-muted);
		font-size: 9px;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.16em;
	}

	.section-content h2,
	.feature-copy h2,
	.visual-heading h2 {
		max-width: 900px;
		margin: 0;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(34px, 4vw, 56px);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.08;
		letter-spacing: -0.035em;
	}

	.two-column-text {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: clamp(40px, 7vw, 110px);
		max-width: 1100px;
		margin-top: 42px;
	}

	.two-column-text p,
	.wide-copy,
	.feature-copy > p,
	.visual-heading > p {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 15px;
		line-height: 1.8;
	}

	.wide-copy {
		max-width: 800px;
		margin-top: 38px;
	}

	.secondary-copy {
		margin-top: 18px;
		color: var(--light-muted);
	}


	/* MUTED SECTION */

	.muted-section {
		background: #eeeeeb;
	}


	/* PROCESS */

	.process-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
		gap: 0;
		margin-top: 60px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.process-item {
		min-height: 280px;
		padding: 28px;
		border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.process-item:last-child {
		border-right: 0;
	}

	.process-item > span {
		color: var(--accent-text);
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 24px;
	}

	.process-item h3 {
		margin: 42px 0 13px;
		font-size: 17px;
	}

	.process-item p {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 13px;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}


	/* FEATURE SECTION */

	.feature-section {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 0.75fr 1.25fr;
		gap: clamp(50px, 8vw, 130px);
		align-items: center;
		padding: 110px var(--page-padding);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.feature-copy > p:not(.eyebrow) {
		margin-top: 25px;
	}

	.feature-image {
        width: 100%;
        max-width: 650px;
        margin: 0;
        justify-self: end;
	}

    .feature-image figcaption {
        margin-top: 14px;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 14px;
        line-height: 1.5;
    }

	.small-image img {
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: 12px;
	}

	figcaption {
		margin-top: 12px;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 14px;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}


	/* FEATURES */

	.feature-list {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		gap: 0;
		margin-top: 55px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-left: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.feature-list div {
		min-height: 135px;
		padding: 22px;
		border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.feature-list span {
		color: var(--accent-text);
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 20px;
	}

	.feature-list p {
		margin: 27px 0 0;
		font-size: 13px;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}


	/* LARGE VISUAL SECTIONS */

	.visual-section {
		padding: 110px var(--page-padding);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.visual-heading {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.7fr;
		gap: 70px;
		align-items: end;
		margin-bottom: 55px;
	}

	.large-visual {
        max-width: 1500px;
        margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.large-visual img {
        width: 100%;
        height: auto;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        background: white;
	}

	.comparison-section {
		background: #eeeeeb;
	}


	/* TECHNOLOGY */

	.dark-section {
		background: #0b100e;
		color: white;
		border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
	}

	.dark-section .section-number {
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
	}

	.tech-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
		margin-top: 55px;
		border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
		border-left: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
	}

	.tech-grid > div {
		min-height: 175px;
		padding: 25px;
		border-right: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
	}

	.tech-grid span {
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.42);
		font-size: 9px;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.15em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.tech-grid h3 {
		margin: 34px 0 7px;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 26px;
		font-weight: 400;
	}

	.tech-grid p {
		margin: 0;
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
		font-size: 12px;
	}


	/* OUTCOME */

	.outcome-section {
		padding-bottom: 130px;
	}

	.takeaway {
		max-width: 900px;
		margin-top: 75px;
		padding-top: 28px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.takeaway > p:last-child {
		max-width: 800px;
		margin: 0;
